AI & Machine Learning Engineering Knowledge Base

1. Machine Learning Basics:
- Supervised Learning: Model is trained on labeled data (e.g., Regression, Classification).
- Unsupervised Learning: Model finds hidden patterns in unlabeled data (e.g., K-Means Clustering, PCA).
- Overfitting: When a model learns noise in training data. Solution: Regularization, Dropout, Cross-validation.

2. RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) & Vector Search:
- RAG combines retrieval systems with generative LLMs to answer queries using custom data.
- Text Chunking: Splitting large text into smaller chunks using RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter.
- Embeddings: Converting text into high-dimensional vector representations.
- Vector DB: FAISS, ChromaDB, and Pinecone store embeddings for fast semantic similarity search.

3. Evaluation Metrics:
- Precision: True Positives / (True Positives + False Positives). Focuses on accuracy of positive predictions.
- Recall: True Positives / (True Positives + False Negatives). Focuses on capturing all positive cases.
- F1-Score: Harmonic mean of Precision and Recall.
